SHA verified against `context.json` and the supplied value before reading. Four sibling perspective files appeared in the directory while I worked; I did not open them.

**Verdict:** `revise` — trust strained, value high, delight clear_hit. **5 blockers, 7 concerns.**

**Core diagnosis:** the sympathetic reading is mostly earned and partly manufactured, and the seam is visible. The origin thesis rests on an exact, verified, first-person quote and holds up. But at four points the draft quotes a source and silently drops the clause where Burr de-escalates his own trauma or marks a joke — the driveway ("But it wasn't a big deal back then"), the wall threat ("He never did it. It's just an empty threat"), the psilocybin setback, and the helicopter's conspiracy-comedy register. Any one is compression; four in the same direction is a thumb on the scale, and two are in Ferriss transcripts the draft itself cites.

**Strongest hit (CRITIC-H1):** "Cross has a real point and it deserves to stay on the table," paired with "That is the reflex. It does not settle whether Cross is right about the money." The genre norm is to use psychology to dissolve the moral question; this draft explicitly refuses. Those two sentences are load-bearing for the article's honesty and must survive any length trim.

**Highest-priority blocker (CRITIC-B1):** the Riyadh centerpiece omits that Burr calls the same gig "one of my top three gigs of all time" and "that one was a great one," inside a run of favorite international gigs. The section sells the passage as a private admission; the source is a war story told as a highlight. The packet independently flags this as the draft's highest-leverage omission.

**Highest-priority concern (CRITIC-C1):** §5 omits HRW's October follow-up (the comedians stayed silent on detained activists) *and* Burr's substantive defense ("They're not gonna progress with isolation"), and picks the dismissive of two published continuations of the "sanctimonious" line. Notably, that second omission cuts against Burr — it makes him look more purely reflexive than the record supports, because pure reflex is what the thesis needs.

Two findings came from my own research rather than the packet: the closing beat's "crisis counselor" is an image handler prepping Zuckerberg for congressional testimony, not a therapist (Wikipedia lists only "Charlie," no role), so the invented chair-and-talking-down scene is unsupported; and the Gina Carano defense — which sits inside the very THR interview supplying the draft's central quote — is absent from both the draft and the evidence packet, in a section arguing political continuity from 2020 to 2025.
